course: dictionary
lesson: 5476
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lash is one word with several meanings, so the context tells you which one you need. Look at the words around it. «Rain lashed the windows» means rain hit the glass hard, again and again. It does not mean the rain was tied up.
explain: Lash can be a thing (a noun) or an action (a verb). «She has long lashes» uses lashes as a noun: these are the small hairs on the edge of your eyelid. «Waves lashed the rocks» uses lashed as a verb, so it describes something that happens.
explain: Ask yourself what the sentence is about. Is it about eyes, weather, a whip, rope, or someone's anger? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense. «Lash out» is a phrase with its own meaning: to suddenly attack or shout at someone in anger.
fact: Lash can be a noun (a lash, lashes) or a verb (lash, lashed, lashing).
fact: An eyelash is one of the small hairs on the edge of your eyelid, and eyelashes help protect your eyes from dust.
fact: «Rain lashed the windows» means rain hit the windows hard and repeatedly.
fact: To lash something can also mean to tie it tightly with rope.
fact: «Lash out» means to suddenly attack or shout at someone in anger, so when you feel cross, take a breath first.
exercise: «Her eyelashes were long and dark.» What is a lash in this sentence? | *An eyelash, one of the small hairs on your eyelid | A rope tied tightly around a box | A whip | A shout of anger
exercise: «Waves lashed against the rocks all night.» What does lashed mean? | Gently stroked | Quietly hidden | Tied tightly | *Hit hard and repeatedly
exercise: Dad tells Ben, «Don't lash out when you are cross.» What does lash out mean? | Wave a hand gently | Tie a bag shut | Fall fast asleep | *Suddenly attack or shout at someone in anger
test: A cat lashes its tail while being stroked. What does this most likely show? | Hunger and a wish for food | *Annoyance, so you should stop stroking it | Happiness at being picked up | Sleepiness
test: «Lashing rain» means rain that is | Made of tiny hairs | Sweet and sticky | Gentle and warm | *Very heavy and falling hard
exam: «He lashed the rope around the boxes so they would not fall.» What does lashed mean here? | Brushed off the dust | Hit hard with a whip | Shouted at in anger | *Tied tightly with rope
